    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0826" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3091: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-01T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 1—9:53
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>419. Bennett<anchor n="81" xml:id="d756-f1"/> advises he and French bank have
                    been approached by the Chinese Government to loan one million each as advance on
                    additional customs surplus famine relief authorized by Department’s telegram
                    271, October 8, 5 p.m. Chinese Government needs this money immediately for
                    famine purposes. Loan does not appear to be within the scope of the consortium.
                    Bennett has received authorization from New York to make loan and has asked
                    Legation’s views. Legation is indicating its approval. Security seems ample and
                    loan would enhance prestige of bank and create favorable impression towards
                    America in China. Negotiations will be concluded in the absence of contrary
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d756-f1" n="81" xml:id="d756-f1-content">
                <p>C. R. Bennett, manager, International Banking Corp., Peking; representative of
                    the American group.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
